WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.874
"How Much Licorice Is Safe?"

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.400
The three ways to alleviate the
fattening effects of stress are:

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.480
#1: treat the cause
by alleviating the stress.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.060
If that's not possible,
you can #2,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.940
modify your diet
to lower the production

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.340
of the adrenal stress hormone
cortisol,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.960
as I describe in my video

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.480
on the effect of animal protein
on adrenal function.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.420
And if all else fails,
you can #3,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.900
try to block the effects
of cortisol on our fat cells.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.360
If you drip cortisol
onto fat samples

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.940
taken deep inside people
undergoing abdominal surgery,

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.840
you can accelerate the formation
and growth of new fat cells.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.880
But you can
disrupt this process

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.980
with a compound
that blocks the enzyme

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.080
that activates cortisol
in body fat.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.380
The compound is called
glycyrrhetinic acid,

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.480
which is what
our gut bacteria make

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.980
and ferry into our bloodstream

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.660
when we eat glycyrrhizin.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.160
Any guess as to where in our
diet glycyrrhizin is found?

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.000
I'll give you a hint: it derives
from the Greek words glykos,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.880
meaning sweet,
and rhiza, meaning root.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.120
We may be able to block some
of the effects of cortisol

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.360
in our body fat
when we eat licorice.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.520
What works to slim
fat cells in a petri dish

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.200
or mice in a lab

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.820
may not work in a person,

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.580
but the licorice compound
appears to work

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.220
even when just
applied to the skin.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.420
Researchers in Italy tried
rubbing the licorice compound

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.960
on women's thighs to see if it
would help with cellulite.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.520
After a month of application,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:41.580
the thickness of the superficial
fat layer on their thighs,

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:42.780
as measured by ultrasound,

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.120
was significantly reduced.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.480
The reason we know it wasn't
just due to massaging it in

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.940
is because there was no change
on the control thigh

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.760
or among the women
that rubbed on placebos.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.580
The difference was
only a few millimeters,

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.680
but the researchers
suggested it could be

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.800
a "gentler alternative
to cosmetic surgery."

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.820
What about eating licorice
or drinking licorice tea?

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.800
Dozens of trials
have been published

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.020
on the effects of various
licorice preparations

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.040
on weight loss,

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.320
and overall there's
just a small effect--

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.020
about a pound of extra weight
loss over a month or two

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:16.980
compared to placebo.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.560
One reason it may not be higher

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.640
is that licorice causes you to
lose body fat but retain water.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:24.660
Check this out.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.460
After 2 months on licorice,

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.020
no change in overall weight--

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.840
but the women dropped
their percentage fat mass

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.100
by nearly 3 percent,

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:35.400
at the same time, though,
increasing their water retention

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.660
by about the same amount.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.120
Then when they stopped
the licorice,

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:39.960
they lost the water,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.580
but gained back the fat.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.580
Licorice can cause you
to burn so much fat,

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.580
the surface of your abdomen
heats up a degree

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.500
within an hour of consumption,

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.820
but it has the opposite effect
on cortisol in your kidneys,

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.620
which, it turns out,
is actually a problem.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.240
In body fat,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.360
licorice blocks an enzyme
that activates cortisol;

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.720
but in our kidneys, licorice
blocks a different enzyme

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.400
that deactivates cortisol,

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.340
causing your kidneys to hold on
to extra water and sodium

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.200
and to lose potassium.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.820
If you lose too much potassium,

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.340
it can cause weakness
and abnormal heart rhythms,

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.700
which is why the FDA sent out
a consumer advisory warning:

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.560
"If you're 40 or older,

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.140
eating 2 ounces
of black licorice a day

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.100
for at least two weeks

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.420
could land you in the hospital

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.060
with an irregular
heart rhythm.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.380
No matter what your age,

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.960
don't eat large amounts
of black licorice at one time.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.420
If you have been eating
a lot of black licorice

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.920
and have
an irregular heart rhythm

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:35.760
or muscle weakness,

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.320
stop eating it immediately

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.360
and contact your
healthcare provider."

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.140
Just because licorice is one
of the oldest and most popular

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.580
herbal medicines in the world

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.120
doesn't mean it's safe to eat
in large amounts

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.760
The retention
of fluid and sodium

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.800
can lead to blood pressure
elevation

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.260
eating less than two ounces
of licorice a day.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.140
The regular consumption
of just a few ounces a day

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.840
can land you in the hospital
in a coma

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.320
with a blood pressure
of 200/140.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.700
As many as 3 percent

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.740
of hospitalizations
due to high blood pressure

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.780
are caused by licorice.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.640
Those with hypertension

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.980
should probably avoid
licorice completely,

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.600
as should pregnant women,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.580
as licorice use
during pregnancy

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.620
is associated
with preterm delivery

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.660
and infant cognitive
dysfunction.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.680
For nonpregnant individuals
with normal blood pressure,

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.140
what would be a safe dose?

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.660
The problem is
glycyrrhizin levels vary

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.220
in different licorice products

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:35.280
and some people are more
sensitive than others.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.640
Now, a lot of licorice
sold in the US

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.860
doesn't even have
any true licorice,

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.840
and is instead
artificially flavored

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.220
or cut with anise oil.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.880
So, ironically, it's the
black licorice you might find

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.260
at a natural food store

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.300
that may pose
the greatest concern.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.300
Including
a broad safety factor,

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.120
the European Scientific
Food Committee suggests

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.060
regular consumption
of no more than 6 grams

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.100
of genuine licorice candy a day.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.500
A Hershey-funded study
found that

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:08.880
"hard-coated licorice candies"
have 0.06 mg/g.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.220
Presuming that's referring
to Good &amp; Plenty,

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.380
the limit would be
about a box a day.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.940
Licorice tea allows you
to access the herb

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.320
without all the crap in candy,

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.600
but a study of 33 brands

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:24.000
found such varying
levels of glycyrrhizin

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.560
that the safe daily dose

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:28.020
ranges from just
a tenth of a cup

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.000
up to 20 cups a day.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.940
A life-threatening
arrhythmia reported

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:36.120
in a case entitled
"Dying for a cup of tea"

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:39.360
was in a woman who was
drinking 15 bags a day.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.640
Based on the average level,

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.000
a half a cup of licorice tea
should be safe for most people,

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.980
though it's not clear
that would be enough

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:48.600
to have a fat-reducing effect,

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.780
which is why licorice
never made it into my book

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.740
"How Not to Diet."

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.940
Finally, cortisol
isn't the only steroid hormone

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.140
licorice can muck with.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.140
It also interferes with
the production of testosterone.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:04.800
Feed men the equivalent of
about 50 boxes of Good &amp; Plenty,

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.480
9 ounces of black licorice,

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:09.960
or just a tablespoon of
licorice root powder every day,

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.120
and they experience
a 44 percent drop

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.760
in testosterone levels
within 4 days,

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:18.420
though blood levels bounced back
within 4 days of stopping.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:21.480
The researchers suggest men
with high blood pressure

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.100
or decreased libido

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.860
should be questioned
about their licorice habits.

